  m_OnCullStateChanged:
    m_PersistentCalls:
      m_Calls: []
  m_text: "This End of Degree Project has been designed and developed by Alicia Ulierte
    Ar\xE9valo, student of Biomedical Engineering at Universidad Rey Juan Carlos,
    under the academic tutorship of Prof. David Rold\xE1n \xC1lvarez.\n\nThe main
    objective of this project is to create a Virtual Reality (VR) simulation of Magnetic
    Resonance Imaging (MRI) that can be experienced both from the perspective of
    the patient and from the perspective of the technician. On one hand, it aims
    to provide future healthcare professionals and technicians with a safe, interactive
    environment where they can learn the correct workflow, protocols, and procedures
    involved in conducting an MRI scan. On the other hand, it also seeks to familiarize
    patients with the environment of an MRI scanner, helping them understand what
    it feels like to undergo this type of examination, thereby reducing fear, stress,
    or uncertainty before the real medical procedure. \n\nI would like to thank you
    sincerely for taking the time to use and explore this simulation. Your feedback
    is highly valuable and much appreciated. Any comments, suggestions, or concerns
    regarding the project are welcome, as they will help improve future versions
    of this tool.\n\nFor any questions or feedback, please do not hesitate to contact
    me at:\na.ulierte.2021@alumnos.urjc.es\n\nAlicia Ulierte Ar\xE9valo\nDegree in
    Biomedical Engineering\nUniversidad Rey Juan Carlos, 2026"
  m_isRightToLeft: 0
  m_fontAsset: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 8f586378b4e144a9851e7b34d9b748ee, type: 2}
